# 0990 (round 2, design notes D2): write-behind park.
# With TF_GLM_PARK_ASYNC=1, DiskCache.park no longer drains the writer or writes inline, and no longer builds,
# checksums or allocates the file image on the request thread (round 1 froze decode on GPU: per-park whole-image
# host allocation + per-piece checksums there). A staging pool of TF_GLM_PARK_STAGING_GIB (8 GiB a rank) is
# preallocated pinned host memory in DiskCache.__init__; park reserves one extent of the file's size from it
# (first-fit, pure bookkeeping), copies the sections in (D2H synced before park returns), publishes the extent to
# the RAM tier under the pending key, adds the index entry at once, and hands the Writer the job. The Writer
# computes the per-piece checksums and writes the header into the extent, sets the ready event (BEFORE any disk
# I/O: check()/read() serve the complete RAM image while the NVMe write is still running), then pwrites the
# extent, fsyncs, renames, re-keys a private RAM-tier copy to the file's HostTier key, and releases the extent
# back to the pool on success and failure alike. A full pool (or a full queue) drops the park at once:
# stats["skipped"], a log line, nothing indexed. Unset or 0 keeps today's synchronous park exactly.
# x25-id: 0990
# x25-flag: TF_GLM_PARK_ASYNC
